#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""The dashboard's play page (/play/; DASHBOARD.md, Play): its back end. The user, 2026-11-12 ~17:05: "I'd like another
option in the menu that leads to a chess board where I can play against a game against a chosen model in the library
at a chosen ply." dashboard.py serves the page and calls this module; it can also be run for checks:

    python3 leagues/play.py resolve ID[@V]                 the player spec of a library row (makes its own games if needed)
    python3 leagues/play.py move ID[@V] PLY [UCI ...]       the model's move after those moves (argmax), with every value
    python3 leagues/play.py legal [UCI ...]                 the engine's legal moves after those moves
    python3 leagues/play.py deep ID[@V] MAXPLY SECONDS [UCI ...]  deep mode's move (SECONDS 0: no limit), each iteration

What the page plays is what an arena plays (arena.py):
- the model: the library snapshot's file (leagues/library/models/...), else the experiment's;
- its calibration: fitted on the model's own calibration games, as in every arena and experiment. They come from the
  arenas' shared cache (leagues/arenas/.owncal-cache, keyed by arena.own_cache_key) when it holds them; otherwise
  they are made here exactly as arena.make_own makes them (the experiment's binary and settings, 600 games at depth 1,
  nice 19, one thread), so they are the games any arena would make;
- the player: cal:<own games>:<kind>:<model> at the chosen ply, in models/from-scratch/bin/chessai-play2 (chessai-play1's
  `play-serve`, whose op=move is the move a tournament player chooses, selfplay::choose_in, byte for byte), the log-odds
  argmax by default, or the arenas' log-odds softmax at T 0.02 (seeded).

Deep mode (2026-11-12 ~18:20; the user: "i'd like to be able to set it to a very high ply", then "let's say up to 10"):
play2's op=deep, iterative deepening of the same search up to a max ply (1-10) within a think time (5 s to 5 min, or no
limit), with a transposition table (96 MiB, fixed) and, if asked, pondering ("think on my time": after its move the
engine searches the position after the reply it predicts; a hit goes on from there). Each completed iteration chooses as
the tournament player of its depth would; the move played is the deepest completed one's. It runs as a job (deep_start,
deep_poll, deep_stop); the page polls it, and a job nobody polls for DEEP_ORPHAN_S is stopped.

Writes only under leagues/play-games/: finished games as PGN, and owncal/<key>/, the own games it had to make (or copy
from the shared cache). Everything else is read. One engine process (nice 19, one thread) answers one request at a
time.
"""
